    <fr:title text="Build prismatizer-style vocal harmonizer in SuperCollider">Build prismatizer-style vocal harmonizer in SuperCollider</fr:title>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>Learn SuperCollider's text-based syntax for writing custom synths and effects. Build a prismatizer-style vocal harmonizer in SuperCollider by studying how it's been reverse-engineered in other DAWs using pitch detection, harmonic layering, and effects processing. Expose that as a reusable instrument for TidalCycles.</html:p>
    <html:p>Initial implementation complete but sounds poor. See <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[sss-0081]]></fr:tex> for detailed findings. Key blocker: <html:code>PitchShift.ar</html:code> is too crude for vocal harmonization, and synthesized vocals don't sound human. Need real vocal input (recorded samples or live mic) and possibly formant-preserving pitch shifting.</html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
